---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { org, donate } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Refund & Cancellation Policy"
  description={`How ${org.name} handles donation refunds, cancellations and recurring giving.`}
  updated="7 September 2026"
>
  <p>
    We want every contribution to be intentional. If something has gone wrong with your donation, tell
    us and we will put it right.
  </p>

  <h2>Donations are generally non-refundable</h2>
  <p>
    Once a donation is received it is committed to programme work, so donations are normally
    non-refundable. The exceptions below are the situations where we will refund.
  </p>

  <h2>When we will refund</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A duplicate transaction caused by a technical or banking error.</li>
    <li>An amount debited that differs from the amount you authorised.</li>
    <li>A donation made in error, where you notify us within 7 days of the transaction date.</li>
    <li>An unauthorised transaction, once verified with your bank.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={org.emailHref}>{org.email}</a> or write to
    <a href={"mailto:" + donate.bank.email}>{donate.bank.email}</a> with your name, the transaction
    date, the amount, and the bank reference number. Call {org.phone} if you would rather speak to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Processing time</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We acknowledge every refund request within 3 working days.</li>
    <li>Approved refunds are processed within 7 to 10 working days.</li>
    <li>Refunds are returned to the original payment method or bank account only.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tax exemption certificates</h2>
  <p>
    If a tax exemption certificate has already been issued for a donation that is later refunded, the
    certificate is cancelled and you must not claim it. We notify you in writing when this happens.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancelling recurring donations</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop a standing instruction at any time through your bank. Tell us as well so we can update
    our records. Amounts already collected before cancellation are not refunded, except under the
    conditions listed above.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
